2 — sh.oo NATIVE fs_*
---

What changed
  `std/sh.oo` is 248 lines. `sh_arg_ok` is in the file (whitelist:
  letters, digits, `/ . - _ = : +` space).
  `sh_mkdir_p(fw: &FsWriteCap, …)` returns `fs_mkdir_p(fw, dir)`.
  `sh_copy(fr, fw, …)` returns `fs_copy_tree(fr, fw, src, dst)`.
  `sh_basename` / `sh_dirname` / `sh_realpath` are pure string folds
  (ProcessCap unused; signature freeze).
  `std/os/fs.oo` is 169 lines. New helpers: `fs_mkdir_p` (linear
  prefix mkdir) and `fs_copy_tree` (recurse + `fs_copy_file`).
  DE1 leftover hunt: `sh_mkdir_p(p` = 0; `sh_copy(p,` = 0. Live
  callers already pass `fw` / `fs`. HARN isolated check: sh.oo OK
  0.40s; fs.oo OK 0.14s. DE2 same fs check OK 0.15s.

Why it matters
  Two mutate ops left the shell. mkdir no longer does `mkdir -p` +
  user string. copy no longer does `cp -r`. Caps are the write/read
  tokens, not ProcessCap.

What is not done
  Sixteen `process_exec` sinks remain in sh.oo: clean (`rm -rf`),
  chmod, git clone, tar extract, chmod_recursive (`find -exec`),
  sleep, curl, which, env_get, env_get_or, md5sum, sha256sum, diff,
  grep, tempfile. git / tar / chmod stay shell after `sh_arg_ok`.
  That class cannot stop option inject, path slip, or hooks
  (sprint_sec_sh.oot still names the hole; the pre-DE1 "gate absent"
  half of that file is stale).
  No `fs_rmdir` / remove_tree. `sh_clean` is still `rm -rf`.
  `fs_mkdir_p` always returns Ok(void) after swallowed prefix Err.
  `fs_copy_tree` has no depth cap and no cycle set. MEM: same class
  as `fs_walk`. `stat` follows symlinks.
  `cap_builtin_ret` maps `fs_mkdir` / `fs_walk`, not `fs_mkdir_p` /
  `fs_copy_tree`. Annotated use of the new names is a table-build
  trigger.
  `sh_arg_ok` allows space, `=`, `:`, `/`. Empty string is true.
  Not a rail-name gate. Not a seal.

Peer
  Current: sprint_de1_mkdir_leftover.oot ZERO leftovers;
  sprint_de2_fs.oot PASS; sprint_harn_fs_check.oot check PASS;
  sprint_mem_b6_fs.oot mkdir_p not walk, copy_tree is walk;
  sprint_hyg_four.oot line lock PASS (sh 248, fs 169).
  Stale: sprint_sec_sh.oot (said `sh_arg_ok` absent);
  sprint_int_prove.oot row 4 (same);
  sprint_residuals_rollup.oot DE10 "gate not landed."

